---
// The example session on the home page, from a real run with jkit 0.5.0 and the hook installed with
// --auto-switch, jdk 17 zulu installed before (paths shortened to ~; the download progress, the
// JKIT_* bookkeeping lines and use's "only this shell" note left out).
// Kept out of the MDX page so Markdown doesn't read the ~ pairs as strikethrough.
---

<pre class="term" aria-label="Example terminal session"><span class="p">$ </span><span class="c">jkit install jdk@21</span>
downloading jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin from github.com
installed jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin → ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin
<span class="d">  signature checked: signed by Adoptium (key 843C48A565F8F04B)
  make it the default: jkit use jdk@21 --global</span>
<span class="p">$ </span><span class="c">cd ~/src/app</span>
jkit: using ~/src/app/jkit.toml: jdk 17.0.21.1+2 zulu
<span class="d">  set    JAVA_HOME=~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu
  PATH   + ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu/bin</span>
<span class="p">$ </span><span class="c">jkit use jdk@21</span>
using jdk 21.0.13.1+2 temurin in this shell
<span class="d">  set    JAVA_HOME=~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin
  PATH   + ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/21.0.13.1+2-temurin/bin
  PATH   - ~/.jkit/tools/jdk/17.0.21.1+2-zulu/bin
  overrides jkit.toml's jdk 17 zulu in this shell; jkit reset jdk to go back to it</span></pre>
